he Tonle Sap and the Mun River valley\' \'According to Coedes, this powerful kingdom, which eventually covered a territory almost equal in extent to that of the later Khmer Empire, subsequently divided itself into a \'Land Zhenla\' that included most of Cambodia and the Khorat Plateau, and a \'Water Zhenla\', centered on the Delta.\''}], {'usage.total_tokens': 2286, 'temperature': 0.2})
