e of Central Thailand, which was formerly a Mon territory."<br>King Rama Khamheng\'s authority "extended down the valley of the Chaophraya and into the Malay peninusula." <br>A Thai prince from the Chiengmai kingdom of northern Thailand married the daughter of the Mon ruler and thus inherited his kingdom. Since the capital was shifted from U-thong to Ayuthia [Skt. Ayodhya] located on an island in the Menam River, this kingdom came to be known as Dvaravati Sri Ayuthia. The weakness of the Sukhothai kingdom gave rise to another Thai State in the north, in the upper region of the upper Mekong. This kingdom came to be known as Lan Chang [now Luang Prabhang]."<br>"The original territory encompassed within the Sukhothai Kingdom was quite limited, confined to the region surrounding the city-provinces of Sukhothai and Sri Satchanalai. However by the last quarter of the 13th century, the kingdom had expanded to many times its..."'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1912, 'temperature': 0.2})
